{"skill":{"slug":"todo-management","displayName":"Todo management"},"version":{"version":"1.1.3","createdAt":1770767608019,"changelog":"No changes in this release.  \n- Version bumped to 1.1.3 without file or documentation updates.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"scripts/todo.sh","size":10443,"sha256":"d1b609ee00cfaca73cb512295f2ee165ae69f5911c268295cff20f860656a5ff","contentType":"text/x-sh"},{"path":"README.md","size":2950,"sha256":"cf7b4c66e73bf0630c257b4e36168a4b02946566870f9b5b8b3b55b5d06268b9","contentType":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4429,"sha256":"c17dfe3e050c47a8467809a57bb69c22083febd2a68cedc9719e8ac522eea8af","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1950,"sha256":"cec0f46f415f6ca2080f5ed20e8d58e38d021e25175aedd539f0edd1960eb0c3","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789030745698,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"648e840a321becc4932fe21aa65d7364b8cba57c918f5aaad519342e825808a9","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/648e840a321becc4932fe21aa65d7364b8cba57c918f5aaad519342e825808a9","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: todo-management\nVersion: 1.1.3\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. The `SKILL.md` explicitly defines strict rules for the AI agent, including 'No file writing (ever)' and 'Never print the todo list unless explicitly asked', which are security-enhancing instructions. The `scripts/todo.sh` script is well-written, employing `sql_q` for proper SQL string escaping and `require_int` for ID validation, effectively mitigating SQL injection vulnerabilities. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the agent for harmful purposes. The functionality is limited to managing a local SQLite database as described.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161106167},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789030745698},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a local todo-list skill whose file access and deletion behavior are disclosed, scoped to its own SQLite todo database, and user-directed.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script defaults to ./todo.db in the current workspace and supports a disclosed TODO_DB override; this is proportionate for a workspace todo manager.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation guidance only asks the user to make the bundled script executable and requires sqlite3; there is no remote fetch, package install, auto-run hook, or hidden setup.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are strict about using only the bundled CLI, keeping replies short, and asking before group deletion with --delete-entries; README could warn more clearly that this flag deletes todo entries.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Persistence is limited to the todo SQLite database, with no system services, scheduled tasks, credential access, privilege escalation, or cross-session agent behavior changes.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's purpose is to manage per-workspace todos in SQLite, and the script implements matching create, list, edit, move, status, remove, and group commands without unrelated capabilities.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a skill creating and modifying a local todo.db in each workspace. Be careful with remove, clear, and group remove --delete-entries because they delete todo entries from that database.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The --delete-entries option can delete todo entries, but that capability is purpose-aligned, scoped to the todo database, and the main SKILL.md instructs the agent to use it only after explicit user choice; the README would benefit from a clearer warning.\n[AIG-SARIF-results] expected: The supplied static scan reported no T01-T09 findings, which is consistent with the inspected artifacts showing no network retrieval, persistence hooks, tool hijacking, or credential handling.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789030745698}}}}}